# src/tychoc.c:6569 -- calling something that is not a function.
# NO `# expect:` on purpose: this lane scores the expectation against ./tychoc1,
# and the two compilers word this one differently -- ./tychoc says
# `calling a value that isn't a function (int)`, ./tychoc1 says
# `this value has type int, not a procedure -- it cannot be called`. They share
# no substring worth asserting, so this fixture is scored on the verdict alone.
fn main():
    xs := [1, 2]
    println(str(xs[0](3)))
